      "observed": "On the root sheet, U2 has global labels SWDIO on PA13, SWCLK on PA14 and SWO on PB3. The J1 Tag-Connect symbol has pins named SWDIO, SWCLK and SWO, but those pins are not connected by wires or by matching global labels to the MCU SWD nets; only J1 GND and VCC have power symbols attached.",
      "expected": "The specification describes J1 as the SWD/JTAG programming header and says its pins are VCC, GND, ~{RESET}, SWCLK, SWDIO, SWO, so the connector pins must share the corresponding MCU SWD nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet: U2 labels 'SWDIO', 'SWCLK', 'SWO'; J1 pins 'SWDIO', 'SWCLK', 'SWO' are not wired or labelled to those nets."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Its pins are VCC, GND, ~{RESET}, SWCLK, SWDIO, SWO — a standard ARM debug/programming interface"}
      ],
      "impact": "A Tag-Connect programmer would not be connected to the MCU SWD signals, making programming/debugging through J1 fail or be unreliable.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J1", "U2", "R10"],
      "pins": ["J1.RESET", "U2.NRST"],
      "nets": ["MBST", "NRST"],
      "observed": "The J1 reset pin appears to carry a global label 'MBST' on the root sheet, while the MCU reset net is labelled 'NRST' at U2 pin 7 and pulled up by R10. There is no NRST/RESET label or wire joining the J1 reset pin to the MCU reset net.",
      "expected": "The specification states that NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}); the connector reset pin should be on the same NRST net as the MCU reset pin.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet: MCU label 'NRST' at U2 pin 7 with R10 to VCC; J1 reset pin label 'MBST'."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R10 (10 kΩ) ties NRST to VCC ... NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET})"}
      ],
      "impact": "The programmer cannot assert or observe MCU reset through J1; debug entry and reset control may fail even if the SWD data lines were connected.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.1", "U5.2", "U5.4", "U5.5", "U5.3"],
      "nets": ["TRXJ_XOR_A", "TRXJ_XOR_B", "TRXJ_XOR_Y", "VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "A root-sheet tile shows an additional powered IC U5, part 74LVG1XOR, with global labels TRXJ_XOR_A and TRXJ_XOR_B and an XOR output label.",
      "expected": "The intended Portal design described in the specification contains U2, U3, U4, A2, A1 and J1 only; there is no such logic gate or TRXJ interface in the component table or architecture.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root-sheet tile: 'U5 74LVG1XOR' with labels 'TRXJ_XOR_A' and 'TRXJ_XOR_B'."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Component table lists U2, U3, U4, A2, A1, J1; no U5 or 74LVG1XOR is present."}
      ],
      "impact": "An unneeded powered XOR gate is present. As drawn its signal labels are not connected to the rest of the board, but it is a clear deviation from the intended component set and could indicate tampering or an assembly/sourcing mistake.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains functional deviations: the Tag-Connect SWD header is not connected to the MCU SWD/reset labels, and an unlisted XOR gate U5 appears on the root sheet."
}

